advocates say the city of minneapolis is  helping to write a new chapter for the  black lives matter's movement  in the united states this after the city  council reached a 27 million dollar  settlement in a civil lawsuit with the  family of george floyd friday  following his death in police custody it  comes just weeks before the first  officer charged in the cases  set to stand trial jeff begase has more  this was the moment last may derrick  chauvin with his knee pressed into  george floyd's neck for approximately  nine minutes it sparked a social justice  movement that led to a summer of unrest  and murder charges against chauvin and  now  a unanimous vote in the minneapolis city  council there are 13 eyes  a 27 million dollar settlement for  george floyd's family  on behalf of the entire city council  offer my deepest condolences to the  family of george floyd  the settlement includes 500 000 for the  community at the intersection where  floyd was killed  floyd family attorney ben crump it sends  a message  that the unjust taking of black life  will no longer be written off as trivial  the 27 million dollar amount is one of  the largest known police wrongful death  settlements on record  last year in louisville brianna taylor's  family received just over 12 million  dollars after her death in a botched  raid  the floyd settlement was announced on  the fourth day of jury selection in  chauvin's trial  so far five men and two women have been  seated  if a juror should hear that there is a  27  million dollar settlement with the  family the jury  has to believe that the city would never  pay that kind of money  unless derek tobin were guilty opening  statements in chauvin's trial are said  to begin  at the end of the month for cbs this  morning saturday i'm jeff begues in  washington
 

